  "notes": "USAGE:\n{指揮|しき} is used in both military/organizational and musical contexts. The word carries a sense of authoritative leadership and coordination.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {指揮|しき}を{執|と}る (to take command)\n- {指揮|しき}{官|かん} (commander, commanding officer)\n- {指揮|しき}{者|しゃ} (conductor — in music)\n- {指揮|しき}{棒|ぼう} (conductor's baton)\n- {指揮|しき}{系統|けいとう} (chain of command)\n\nWATCH OUT:\nNot to be confused with 〜{式|しき} (ceremony, style) or {四季|しき} (four seasons), which share the same reading.",
